     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"2\\left( {3a + 5} \\right) + \\left( { - 3} \\right)\\left( {a + 2} \\right)\"></span></td>\n<td>Use the distributive property.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"2\\left( {3a} \\right) + 2\\left( 5 \\right) + \\left( { - 3} \\right)\\left( a \\right) + \\left( { - 3} \\right)\\left( 2 \\right)\"></span></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"6a + 10 - 3a - 6\"></span></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Like terms are constants or have the same variable and exponent. Group the like terms.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\left( {6a - 3a} \\right) + \\left( {10 - 6} \\right)\"></span></p>\n<p>Add the coefficients and keep the same variable.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"3a + 4\"></span></p>"
    },
